I was playing an early doppelganger tourist, and was feeling pretty
good. I had recently bought a scimitar in a shop for dirt cheap, and
was increasing my skill in it (I've heard somewhere scimitars hit
moderately hard, is this true?). Upon killing a dwarf I find a silver
saber. Glee! I weild the silver saber - and it welds itself to my
hand.

Well, I'm a level four doppelganger, right? I kill two birds with one
stone, polymorphing into a cockatrice to drop the saber and lay an
egg. I leave the egg behind, (paranoid of it flying out of my pack and
killing me in the process), knowing that it will somehow know me its
mother when it hatches. Then I wander off (as I am apt to do),
slashing things clumsily with my unskilled scimitar.

FLASH FORWARD!

After mapping the level, I come back across a room to find a goblin.
Easy kill! Maybe this will be the one to bring me up to basic in
scimitar! As I move forward - it throws an egg at me! Why, that little
punk -

You feel yourself slowing down.

He threw a cockatrice egg at me!

Well, it all ended well. I prayed, he only had one egg and it didn't
last long after that. I was wondering where in hell he got the egg
when I remembered my unhatched pet. Aww, now that's not nice...

Oh, and in case you were wondering...yes, he was the one to bring me
to basic. :)

